    "description": "<p><i>Reference Book:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Star_Wars_Saga_Edition_Scavenger%27s_Guide_to_Droids\" title=\"Star Wars Saga Edition Scavenger's Guide to Droids\">Star Wars Saga Edition Scavenger's Guide to Droids</a></i></p><p>Some automated security systems check biometric data before granting access to an area. <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Droids\" title=\"Droids\">Droids</a> cannot provide retinal scans, fingerprints, or other unique biological features. The ID Dodge simulates such information, allowing a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Droid\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Droid\">Droid</a> to access secure areas. This <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Droid_Accessory\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Droid Accessory\">Droid Accessory</a> allows the <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Droid\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Droid\">Droid</a> to use a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Deception\" title=\"Deception\">Deception</a> check instead of a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Use_Computer\" title=\"Use Computer\">Use Computer</a> check on any security device that requires organic biometric identification.</p>",
    "source": "Star Wars Saga Edition Scavenger's Guide to Droids",
